<title>SINGAPORE: India 0.25-pct diesel offers at plus $2.50-$2.90.</title>
<headline>India 0.25-pct diesel offers at plus $2.50-$2.90.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Offers into state-owned Indian Oil Corp's (IOC) October-delivery import tender for 0.25 percent sulphur diesel ranged between $2.50 and $2.90 per barrel over MidEast quotes, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The two 45,000-tonne cargoes that IOC sought are for October 11-15 delivery, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to the west coast, they said.</p>
<p>The tender closed on September 12 and would be awarded later this evening.</p>
<p>In its last tender for September arrival, IOC bought two 45,000-tonne cargoes of 0.25 percent sulphur diesel at $2.88 per barrel over MidEast quotes, c-and-f west coast and 90 cents per barrel on a free-on-board (fob) basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (+65-8703084)</p>
